      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "It should be noted that the ambient gradient should also be added to this script, [Ambient Sky/Equator/Ground Color], think it should be possible to change between the types on the fly at runtime but not entirely sure about that, though adding a dropdown menu to change between the fucntions could be user friendly.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2019-01-15T03:44:22.289Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "So... we are missing the last piece of the puzzle in day and night cycle for maps, Ambient Light has been an hinder for many, and using realtime skybox is usually not an option as it creates a whole lot of extra work and you may not want to use that specific Skybox for the environment light effect you want to create.\n\nAnd as we are missing the ability to Edit the Lighting Tab in Unity we are in need of going the script way, so i added Example (GIF) and the reference script (Picture 1) that is running with a animation showing it should be possible to add ingame as realtime animating lighting settings.\n\nSo our request is for VRChat to create a basic script for us to use, this so we can use the whitelisted asset for control over the lighting Tab via Animations.\n\nThere may be more settings and parameters from the Lighting Tab that could be of interest adding to this Script, i hope the comments can pinpoint them out. :)\n\nIl add a reference to Unity Documents also:\nhttps://docs.unity3d.com/2017.4/Documentation/ScriptReference/RenderSettings-ambientLight.html",
